 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "s3_p01",
   "conversationId": "s3_drift:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "What's the difference between supervised and unsupervised learning?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:02:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s3_p02",
   "conversationId": "s3_drift:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "Why do we need a separate test set if we already have a validation set?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:04:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s3_p03",
   "conversationId": "s3_drift:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "What is overfitting and how can I tell it's happening from the loss curves?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:06:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s3_p04",
   "conversationId": "s3_drift:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "Can you explain the bias-variance tradeoff with a simple example?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:08:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s3_p05",
   "conversationId": "s3_drift:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "How does k-fold cross-validation work?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:10:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s3_p06",
   "conversationId": "s3_drift:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "Is accuracy a bad metric for imbalanced classes? What should I use instead?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:12:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s3_p07",
   "conversationId": "s3_drift:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "Why does L1 regularization give sparse weights but L2 doesn't?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:14:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s3_p08",
   "conversationId": "s3_drift:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "What problem do recurrent neural networks solve that feedforward ones don't?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:16:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s3_p09",
   "conversationId": "s3_drift:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "Why do LSTMs have gates? What's the forget gate for?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:18:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s3_p10",
   "conversationId": "s3_drift:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "What's the problem with RNNs on long sentences?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:20:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s3_p11",
   "conversationId": "s3_drift:c2",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "What is attention in seq2seq models? The decoder 'looks at' the encoder states?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:22:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s3_p12",
   "conversationId": "s3_drift:c2",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "In self-attention, what are queries, keys and values? Where do they come from?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:24:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s3_p13",
   "conversationId": "s3_drift:c2",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "Why do we divide by sqrt(d_k) in scaled dot-product attention?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:26:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s3_p14",
   "conversationId": "s3_drift:c2",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "How does the transformer know the word order if attention is permutation invariant?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:28:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s3_p15",
   "conversationId": "s3_drift:c2",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "Why sinusoidal positional encodings instead of just learning position embeddings?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:30:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s3_p16",
   "conversationId": "s3_drift:c2",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "What's the point of multi-head attention? Isn't one head enough?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:32:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s3_p17",
   "conversationId": "s3_drift:c2",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "I tried to compute attention weights by hand for 3 tokens: softmax of QK^T. Is each row supposed to sum to 1?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:34:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s3_p18",
   "conversationId": "s3_drift:c2",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "How does the causal mask work in the decoder?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:36:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s3_p19",
   "conversationId": "s3_drift:c2",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "Is the transformer encoder the same as BERT?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:38:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s3_p20",
   "conversationId": "s3_drift:c2",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "How do the heads get combined after multi-head attention, just concatenation?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:40:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s3_p21",
   "conversationId": "s3_drift:c2",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "Why is attention O(n^2) in sequence length? Is that why context windows are limited?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:42:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s3_p22",
   "conversationId": "s3_drift:c2",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "What's the difference between self-attention and cross-attention in the decoder?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:44:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s3_p23",
   "conversationId": "s3_drift:c2",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "Do I add or concatenate the positional encoding to the token embedding?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:46:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s3_p24",
   "conversationId": "s3_drift:c2",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "What does the padding mask do, and how is it different from the causal mask?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:48:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s3_p25",
   "conversationId": "s3_drift:c2",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "Can you quiz me on the transformer architecture? I want to check I understand the whole forward pass.",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:50:00Z"
  }
 ]
}
